{"role":"assistant","content":"Reproduced. Root cause confirmed: `similarity()` returns a Python `float`, and boto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects floats. The first publish succeeds only because the library is empty, so `similar` is `[]` and no float reaches `put_item`. The second publish puts float scores into `similar` → `TypeError` → 500 — and every publish after that fails the same way.\n\nNow the fix in `src/app.py` — store scores as `Decimal`, which is what DynamoDB accepts:","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_wsK15gk89DWka1zUrZRwtai3","function":{"name":"Edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"src/app.py\",\"old_string\":\"import json\\nimport logging\\nimport re\\nimport time\",\"new_string\":\"import json\\nimport logging\\nimport re\\nimport time\\nfrom decimal import Decimal\"}"}}]}
